=================================

The LICENCE in this repository covers material authored for this project. It
does not cover the following, which remains under its own terms.


1. SAMOS 2019 thermal test chip dataset  (REDISTRIBUTED HERE)
-------------------------------------------------------------
File:     validation/measured/ttc_samos2019_steady.json
Licence:  Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC-BY 4.0)
          https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
Source:   F. Terraneo, A. Leva, W. Fornaciari, "An Open-hardware Platform for
          MPSoC Thermal Modeling", 2019 IEEE International Conference on
          Embedded Computer Systems: Architectures, Modeling and Simulation
          (SAMOS).
Dataset:  https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.2871796

What is here is a DERIVED EXTRACT, not the dataset: steady-state averages
taken from the raw 10 Hz traces by tools/ttc_extract.py, with the diode
channel alignment of two recordings corrected (recorded in the file's
"corrections" field). The raw traces are not redistributed; they are at the
DOI above. The extract is used and redistributed under CC-BY 4.0 with the
attribution above, and anyone may use that file under those same terms,
independently of this repository's own licence.


2. Published values cited, not redistributed
--------------------------------------------
Effective material properties in src/composite_materials.py are computed from
constants and equations published in:

  Rao et al., Thermal Science 27(5B), 4193-4207 (2023),
  doi:10.2298/TSCI220805061R

  Zhang et al., "Thermal Characterization of Both Bare Die and Overmolded
  2.5-D Packages on Through Silicon Interposers", IEEE T-CPMT, 2014
  (used in validation/cases/astar-tsi-2p5d-bare-die.json and documented in
  validation/MEASURED_DATA.md)

  The 3D-ICE 3.0 paper (IEEE TCAD 41(4), 2022) is cited in
  validation/MEASURED_DATA.md to pin the test chip's geometry.

Physical constants and equations are facts and are not themselves subject to
copyright; the citations are given so every number can be traced to its source
and checked.


3. Dependencies
---------------
This project depends on, but does not include, the following, each under its
own licence:

  numpy        BSD 3-Clause
  scipy        BSD 3-Clause
  matplotlib   PSF-based (matplotlib licence)
  pytest       MIT

No model weights in data/models/ are derived from third-party data: they are
trained on labels produced by this project's own solver (data/datasets/) and
on text generated by ai/language_corpus.py.
